---
// The BBC Micro: its screen, the controls a person at the machine has (BREAK,
// the sound, the disc drive) and the line that says how fast this browser runs
// it. public/bbc-micro.js brings it to life when the visitor presses Start, and
// downloads nothing before then. Without JavaScript every control is disabled
// and the status line says why.
//
// The canvas starts at the framebuffer's size, 640 by 512 (Framebuffer.Width
// and Height), and the script sets it from the machine once it is loaded. The
// stylesheet shows it in the television's shape, four wide by three high.
//
// The screen is where the keyboard goes: with focus on it, keys type into the
// machine. The script makes it focusable once the machine runs; Tab is never
// taken, so focus can always move on.
//
// Under the screen are the BBC Micro's keys as buttons, in its own layout
// (ON_SCREEN_ROWS in public/bbc-keys.js), for touch and for anyone without the
// keys on their own keyboard. SHIFT and CTRL latch for the next key.
//
// The disc drive has two ways in. The library: a list of preset discs
// (machines/bbc-micro/discs/manifest.json), each credited under the list with
// its author, licence and source, which Insert and run puts in drive 0 and
// starts with SHIFT and BREAK; the image is fetched from this site only then.
// And the visitor's own file: dropped on the page, or chosen with Insert a
// disc, read in the tab and never sent anywhere. A disc from the library is a
// disc like any other once it is in: Save disc downloads it as it stands.
import { megabytes } from '../lib/bbc-micro.mjs';
import { discLicenceUrl, discSourceUrl, needsSource } from '../lib/bbc-discs.mjs';
import { ON_SCREEN_ROWS, STICKY, legend, spokenName } from '../../public/bbc-keys.js';

interface Props {
  /** Where the machine's files are served from, /machines/bbc-micro/. */
  base: string;
  /** The machine's clock in MHz, from the registry. */
  clockMhz: number;
  /** The ROM files the page loads, in the order BbcHost.Load takes them. */
  roms: string[];
  /** The bytes the Start button downloads, read from the build, or null when this build has no machine. */
  download: number | null;
  /** The preset discs, from src/lib/bbc-discs.mjs: grouped by kind, and the default. */
  library: { groups: { name: string; discs: any[] }[]; default: any };
}
const { base, clockMhz, roms, download, library } = Astro.props;
---

<div class="bbc" data-bbc data-base={base} data-clock-mhz={clockMhz} data-roms={roms.join(' ')} data-download={download ?? undefined} data-state="static">
  <div class="bbc-screen" data-bbc-screen role="application" aria-label="The BBC Micro's screen" aria-describedby="bbc-typing">
    <canvas data-bbc-canvas width="640" height="512"></canvas>
  </div>
  <p class="bbc-note">The picture is the machine's own, pixel for pixel, as its video chips draw it, shown in the television's shape. It models the picture, not a television: no scan lines, no glow and no curve.</p>
  <p class="bbc-note" id="bbc-typing">With the screen focused, your keyboard types into the BBC Micro, key for key by where the keys are, and the machine's own keys further down type by a tap or a click. Tab moves on, so the page never keeps the keyboard.</p>
  <div class="bbc-controls">
    <button type="button" class="btn pill" data-bbc-start disabled>Start the BBC Micro{download !== null && `, a download of up to ${megabytes(download)} MB`}</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-break disabled>Break</button>
    <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-sound disabled>Turn sound on</button>
  </div>
  <p class="bbc-status" role="status" data-bbc-status>The BBC Micro runs in your browser, and it needs JavaScript to do that. With JavaScript off, the page and the program below are shown, but nothing runs.</p>
  <p class="bbc-line" data-bbc-sound-status aria-live="polite">Sound is off.</p>
  <p class="bbc-speed" data-bbc-speed></p>
  <div class="bbc-keys" role="group" aria-label="The BBC Micro's keys">
    {ON_SCREEN_ROWS.map((row) => (
      <div class={`bbc-keys-row${row.includes('Left') ? ' cursor' : ''}`}>
        {row.map((key) => {
          const words = legend(key).length > 2 && !/^f\d$/.test(legend(key));
          const sticky = STICKY.includes(key);
          return (
            <button type="button" class={`bbc-key${words ? ' word' : ''}${key === 'Space' ? ' space' : ''}`} data-bbc-key={key} aria-label={spokenName(key) === legend(key) ? undefined : spokenName(key)} aria-pressed={sticky ? 'false' : undefined} disabled>{legend(key)}</button>
          );
        })}
      </div>
    ))}
  </div>
  <fieldset class="bbc-disc">
    <legend>The disc drive</legend>
    <div class="bbc-presets" data-bbc-presets>
      <label class="bbc-preset-label" for="bbc-preset">A disc from the library</label>
      <select id="bbc-preset" data-bbc-preset aria-describedby="bbc-preset-about" disabled>
        {library.groups.map((group) => (
          <optgroup label={group.name}>
            {group.discs.map((d) => <option value={d.slug} selected={d === library.default}>{d.title}</option>)}
          </optgroup>
        ))}
      </select>
      <div id="bbc-preset-about" class="bbc-preset-about">
        {library.groups.flatMap((group) => group.discs).map((d) => (
          <div class="bbc-preset-disc" data-bbc-preset-disc={d.slug} data-title={d.title} data-licence={d.licence} hidden={d !== library.default}>
            {d.note && <p class="bbc-preset-note" role="note">{d.note}</p>}
            <p><b>{d.title}</b>, {d.author}, {d.year}. {d.description}</p>
            <p>Keys: {d.controls}.</p>
            <p>Licence: <a href={discLicenceUrl(d)}>{d.licence}</a>. <a href={d.sourceUrl}>The author's page</a>{needsSource(d) && <>, and <a href={discSourceUrl(d)}>its source in the repository</a></>}.</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <div class="bbc-controls">
        <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-preset-run disabled>Insert and run</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-preset-insert disabled>Insert in drive 0</button>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="bbc-controls">
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-insert disabled>Insert a disc</button>
      <input type="file" accept=".ssd,.dsd" data-bbc-file hidden />
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-blank disabled>Make a blank disc</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-save disabled>Save disc</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn small" data-bbc-eject disabled>Eject</button>
      <label class="bbc-protect"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" data-bbc-protect disabled /> Write-protect</label>
    </div>
    <p class="bbc-line" data-bbc-drive aria-live="polite">Drive 0 is empty.</p>
    <p class="bbc-note">Insert and run puts the disc in drive 0 and starts it the way the BBC Micro does, with SHIFT held through BREAK; Insert in drive 0 only puts it in, for <kbd>*CAT</kbd> and <kbd>*RUN</kbd>. The image is fetched from this site when you insert it, not before. A disc from the library goes in writable unless Write-protect is on, so a game can keep its high scores on it: they last until the disc is changed or the page is left, and Save disc keeps them as a file.</p>
    <p class="bbc-note">Or use a disc of your own: drop a .ssd or .dsd disc image on the page, or press Insert a disc. The file is read in this tab and is not uploaded anywhere; Save disc downloads the disc as it now stands, which is the only way to keep what was written to it. The page has drive 0 only: the controller and DFS have a second drive, and the page does not offer it.</p>
    <p class="bbc-note">DFS remembers the catalogue of the last disc it read until the drive stops, a moment after the last disc command, as it does on the real machine. So after changing discs, type <kbd>*CAT</kbd> first, or DFS may still list the old one.</p>
  </fieldset>
</div>
